Port of _patches/typescript/012-ls-hover.patch (tsc/internal/ls/hover.go) to tsrs.

- AfterQuickInfoCallback, RegisterAfterQuickInfoCallback: `tsrs_ls::{AfterQuickInfoCallback,
  register_after_quick_info_callback}` (a `fn` in a process-wide `RwLock`; registering replaces the previous one,
  as in Go). Go passes the program as a `checker.Program` interface holding the `*compiler.Program`; the Rust
  callback takes that `&'static tsrs_compiler::Program` directly.
- ProvideHover calls it after getQuickInfoAndDocumentationForSymbol, before the empty-quickInfo check, and uses
  the range node it returns when there is one.

